{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 37, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3.5-397b-a17b", "content": "the social network is a gripping drama that chronicles the founding of facebook and the subsequent legal battles faced by its creator, mark zuckerberg. directed by david fincher and written by aaron sorkin, the film stands out for its sharp dialogue and rapid pacing. jesse eisenberg delivers a compelling performance as zuckerberg, portraying him as a brilliant but socially awkward individual driven by a desire for recognition and status. the soundtrack, composed by trent reznor and atticus ross, creates a cold, electronic atmosphere that perfectly complements the digital age setting. the narrative unfolds through a series of depositions, jumping between the early days at harvard university and the later lawsuits filed by eduardo saverin and the winklevoss twins. this non-linear structure keeps the audience engaged as pieces of the puzzle come together. the cinematography is sleek and modern, emphasizing the isolation inherent in connecting with others online. themes of betrayal, ambition, and friendship are explored with nuance, showing how success can come at a personal cost. while some details may be dramatized for effect, the core emotional truth of the story resonates deeply. it is not just a movie about a website; it is a study of human nature in the modern world. the film remains a masterpiece of contemporary cinema, offering a timeless look at how technology shapes our relationships and identities.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.13125505}, {"token": " social", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " network", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -1.365982}, {"token": " a", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " gripping", "logprob": -0.17207338}, {"token": " drama", "logprob": -0.085063204}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.0067153242}, {"token": " chron", "logprob": -0.0008155452}, {"token": "icles", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " the", "logprob":